WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.441
In Entra ID, three things decide
what a technician can do:

2
00:00:03.441 --> 00:00:07.495
the role decides the action, the
target decides whether it applies,

3
00:00:07.495 --> 00:00:10.738
and the administrative unit
narrows the population.

4
00:00:10.738 --> 00:00:15.850
The least-privileged role for a non-admin
password reset is Password Administrator.

5
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.877
Authentication Administrator
handles methods

6
00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:21.387
and Temporary Access Passes for members.

7
00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:25.011
Only the Privileged Authentication
Administrator can reset a

8
00:00:25.011 --> 00:00:28.499
privileged administrator, so
that role sits outside the desk.

9
00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:30.475
Capability isn't authority.

10
00:00:30.475 --> 00:00:34.049
Authentication Administrator
can delete and disable users,

11
00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:37.833
and Application Administrator
can grant consent, so the program

12
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:42.037
replaces it with a custom role that
only assigns groups to applications.

13
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:46.963
Executives sit in restricted management
units the general desk can't reach.

14
00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:52.074
Roles reach technicians through
role-assignable groups, eligible through P I M.

15
00:00:52.074 --> 00:00:54.700
And approval isn't identity verification.

16
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.390
The ladder is the CISO's decision:
a phishing-resistant sign-in first;

17
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.763
identity proofing, in person
against a PIV card or

18
00:01:02.763 --> 00:01:06.712
through Entra account recovery,
when every method is lost.

19
00:01:06.712 --> 00:01:11.648
Then a one-time pass with the shortest
lifetime, a notice on a separate channel,

20
00:01:11.648 --> 00:01:15.480
and for high-risk tasks, two
approvers besides the executor.
